# Secrets -- never let these into git history
.env

# Generated at runtime, not source
data/*.jsonl
data/archive/
data/*.txt
data/.gremlin.lock
data/talking.marker
data/.sudo_credential
*.gremlin-backup-*

# Downloaded model weights -- large binaries, not source, and can
# always be re-downloaded via `gremlin models` / `gremlin models --hf`
models/*.gguf

# Standard Python/venv noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
.venv/

# isolated venv + scratch (TMPDIR, HF cache, raw training output) for
# deploy/local-finetune-unsloth.py -- unsloth's own deps would conflict
# with the production venv's torch/transformers pins if installed there,
# so this is a separate, disposable venv. The real script + doc live in
# deploy/; only this scratch working directory is excluded.
.finetune-venv/
.finetune-venv-scripts/

# android/ is part of this same repo now, tracked alongside the
# desktop files -- only its generated build artifacts are excluded,
# same as the desktop side's own venv/__pycache__ exclusions above.
android/.gradle/
android/**/build/

# llama.cpp checkout -- only used for its convert_hf_to_gguf.py +
# quantize tooling when finetune.py promotes a new fine-tuned GGUF,
# not project source. Re-clonable, not something to track.
tools/llama.cpp/

# Per-conversation short-term memory (survives restarts, wiped on 'clear')
data/conversations/
# Runtime data written by research/bench/council -- not source
data/*.json
data/research_queue.jsonl
data/bench_results.jsonl
data/research_results.jsonl

# Fine-tuned checkpoints/merges/GGUFs -- tens of GB, regenerable via
# `gremlin finetune --target=<model>`, never something to push to GitHub.
data/finetunes/

# Curated source content, not runtime output -- exceptions to the
# data/*.txt and data/*.json blanket rules above.
!data/distill_prompts.txt
!data/submodel_base_repos.json

# Timestamped/one-off config backups from maintenance edits -- the real
# history is in git, these are just local safety nets during a change.
config/models.yaml.bak-*

# Magic build: model quality bench runtime output
bench/quality-*.jsonl
scratch_*.py

# zoid loop
data/zoid/
data/zoid_stop

# per-battle transcripts -- local debugging fuel for reflexion, not
# something the nightly commit stages (only data/skills is); left
# untracked they piled up to 500+ files / 34MB uncommitted. Regenerable
# by re-running the battle, not backup-worthy.
data/magic/episodes/
unsloth_compiled_cache/

# Battle working copies -- confirmed live 2026-09-19 to have leaked
# 108 junk commits ("magic: battle start", "step N: edit_file X") into
# THIS repo's real history via a _git_begin() bug (fixed in battle.py,
# see its docstring). Gitignored too, as defense in depth: nothing
# that walks into this directory should ever be able to add its
# contents to the outer repo again, bug or no bug. Regenerable by
# re-running the battle, not backup-worthy.
data/magic/work/

# Daily defense reports (roadmap #96): open ports, unpatched CVEs,
# sshd hardening gaps. Real host security posture -- never belongs in
# git history, pushed to a remote or not. Regenerated daily anyway, so
# nothing lost by not tracking it; the weekly backup (#74) doesn't
# include this directory either, same reasoning.
data/defense/
